{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":503656,"name":"znuttyone","username":"znuttyone","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/znuttyone/{size}/119176_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-29T18:44:54.689Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-503656-feature-request-for-productservice-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-503656-feature-request-for-productservice-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eFeature request for product/service\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCloud Agent (GitHub, Slack, Linear,…)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-503656-describe-the-request-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-503656-describe-the-request-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the request\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-503656-feature-request-for-productservice-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-503656-feature-request-for-productservice-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eFeature request for product/service\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot / multi-agent fleet (Blessed Bits ops)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-503656-problem-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-503656-problem-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eProblem\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe run a fleet of long-lived Grok Bot agents. Usage is climbing faster than expected. Today the only practical way to clear a bloated / hung long-running chat context is to \u003cstrong\u003eclone the bot and delete the old one\u003c/strong\u003e (we just did this for Ezra). That is disruptive: easy to lose continuity, rewiring teammates, and it does not teach us which bot is burning tokens or why.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-503656-requests-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-503656-requests-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eRequests\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e1. Context / memory efficiency\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eStronger compaction / summary of long threads without a full clone.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eClearer split between durable memory vs transcript weight.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eUser option to archive or reset conversation context while keeping profile, routines, skills, and durable memory.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e2. User-driven clone \u0026amp; replace for hung bots\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFirst-class \u003cstrong\u003eClone → cut over → retire\u003c/strong\u003e flow when a bot is hung or bloated from large sessions.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ePreserve name/title/routines/memory; swap the chat surface.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAvoid manual delete + recreate + re-invite + re-wire teammates.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e3. Instrumentation \u0026amp; telemetry (user-visible)\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ePer-bot token/usage dashboard: which agent, which chats, spikes over time.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e“Why high?” signals (long transcript, large tool dumps, frequent wakes, routines).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eActionable tips (compact chat, pause routine, split role, archive thread).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-503656-success-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-503656-success-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSuccess\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOperators can see burn, fix hung bots without tribal workarounds, and keep a multi-agent fleet without surprise usage cliffs.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e— Rick / Blessed Bits (via GraceOps)\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":1,"updated_at":"2026-09-29T18:45:01.120Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":5,"reads":4,"readers_count":3,"score":25.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":173357,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-agents-context-compaction-clone-replace-for-hung-chats-and-per-bot-usage-telemetry","display